===Etymology 2===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*leǵ-}}
From {{bor|en|es|León}}, from {{der|en|la|legiō||[[legion]]}}, named for the {{w|Legio VII Gemina}}, which settled there. In reference to the New York town and Texan river, taken from the former Spanish kingdom. The Texan lake is named for the river. The Floridian county is named for the Spanish explorer {{w|Juan Ponce de Leon}}. The Texan county is named for {{w|Martín De León|Martin de Leon}}, founder of Victoria, Texas. The town in Monroe Co., Wisconsin, was named for the Mexican city. The Iowan town was changed to honor the "Fighting Doctor" of the {{w|Mexican–American War}} {{w|David Camden de Leon}} after it was discovered that Iowa already had a city named {{w|Independence, Iowa|Independence}}. The Kansan town was named for the one in Iowa. {{doublet|en|legion}} via Old French. The California town was named for the nearby Leon Mine.

